{{also|dela|delà|dēlā|dēla}}
==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|LL-Q150 (fra)-Lyokoï-de la.wav|Audio}}

===Article===
{{head|fr|article|head=[[de]] [[la]]|g=f|masculine|du|plural|des}}

# of the
# [[some|Some]]; ''the feminine partitive article''
#: {{uxi|fr|Voudriez-vous '''de la''' confiture ?|Would you like '''some''' jam?}}
#: {{uxi|fr|J'ai mangé '''de la''' tarte|I ate '''some''' pie.}}

====Usage notes====
* While English does have the partitive determiner {{m|en|some}}, the French article {{m|fr||de la}} frequently translates to nothing at all in English; for example, the above example « J'ai mangé '''de la''' tarte » could also be translated simply as “I ate pie.”
* Like the definite article {{m|fr|la}} (from which it derives), the partitive article {{m|fr||de la}} undergoes elision, becoming {{m|fr|de l'-}} before most words that start with vowel sounds.

