==Romanian==

===Etymology===
{{m|ro|de}} + {{m|ro|la}}, {{lit|from at|nocap=1}}.

===Preposition===
{{ro-prep|a}}

# [[from]] {{gloss|spatial, relational, causal}}
#: {{syn|ro|de|din}} {{gloss|not interchangeable}}
#: {{uxi|ro|Au furat ceva '''de la''' casa ta.|They stole something '''from''' your house.}}
#: {{uxi|ro|Am învățat mult '''de la''' tine.|I've learned a lot '''from''' you.}}
#: {{uxi|ro|Am obosit '''de la''' citit.|I'm tired '''from''' reading.}}
#: {{uxi|ro|'''de la''' A la Z|'''from''' A to Z}}
#: {{uxi|ro|'''de la''' distanță|'''from''' afar}}
# [[from]], [[since]] {{gloss|temporal}}
#: {{syn|ro|de|din}} {{gloss|not interchangeable, see notes}}
#: {{uxi|ro|Este treaz '''de la''' ora opt.|He is awake '''since''' eight o'clock.}}
#: {{uxi|ro|'''de la''' început|'''from''' the beginning}}
# [[by]] {{gloss|instrumental}}
#: {{uxi|ro|'''de la''' sine|'''by''' itself}}
# {{n-g|Word to join the parts of a compound; sometimes corresponding to "[[of]]".}}
#: {{syn|ro|de}}
#: {{uxi|ro|buzunar '''de la''' pantalon|pant pocket}}
#: {{uxi|ro|apă '''de la''' robinet|tap water}}
#: {{uxi|ro|abatere '''de la''' lege|breach '''of''' law}}

====Usage notes====
* When constructing phrases of the form "''from X to Y''", it is usually accompanied by "''({{l|ro|până}}) {{l|ro|la}}''": "'''''de la''' X ({{l|ro|până}}) {{l|ro|la}} Y''"

{{sense|since (temporal)}}

'''de la''' is usually used together with a fixed point in time (though not with dates):
: {{uxi|ro|'''de la''' ora nouă|'''since''' nine o'clock}}
: {{uxi|ro|'''de la''' ianuarie|'''since''' January}}
'''din''' is usually used together with dates or in certain expressions:
: {{uxi|ro|'''din''' (anul) 2000|'''since''' (the year) 2000}}
: {{uxi|ro|'''din''' acel moment|'''from''' that moment '''on'''}}
'''de''' is usually used for time frames:
: {{uxi|ro|'''de''' un an|'''for''' a year}}
: {{uxi|ro|'''de''' mult timp|'''for''' a long time}}

